||| Library-side build cell: the primary `(executor, dtype)` for this build,
||| generated by `mk/genconfig.mk` (same sed mechanism as the examples'
||| `BuildConfig.idr` + the library's `HwConfig.idr`). `ML.Simple` re-exports
||| these as `Ex` / `F` so tutorial code writes `Tensor dims Ex F g` and never
||| spells `{ex=}` — the `ExampleExecutor`/`ExampleDType` trick, generalized
||| into the library itself.
|||
||| Spelled as concrete types (not `presetExecutor` typeclass methods) so
||| downstream constraints reduce during elaboration — same reason as
||| `BuildConfig.ExampleExecutor`. Idris-2 can't drive type-level selection
||| from a runtime env var, so the env is observed at build time.
|||
||| Do not edit `ML/Config.idr` directly — it is `.gitignore`d and clobbered
||| each build. Edit this `.in` file instead.
module ML.Config

import public Executor

public export
DefaultExecutor : Type
DefaultExecutor = @EXAMPLE_EXECUTOR_TYPE@

public export
DefaultDType : Type
DefaultDType = @EXAMPLE_DTYPE_TYPE@
